  "step_3": "The decision reason requires the individual to evaluate the skewness of the lotteries, specifically noting that a greater portion of probability is assigned to unfavorable outcomes defines right-skewness, and that the more right-skewed lottery is preferred. In this case, Lottery A has 100% probability of a loss (-500), so it is more right-skewed (more probability on unfavorable outcome) than Lottery B, which has 50% on -1000. Therefore, according to the reason, A should be preferred. However, the verbal report does not mention skewness or the distribution of probability on unfavorable outcomes. Instead, the individual focuses on the 50% chance of avoiding a loss and the value of that chance, which reflects a different reasoning — possibly risk-seeking or risk-averse trade-off — not based on skewness. The individual does not apply the skewness criterion at all. Therefore, the decision reason was not used. The reasoning described is inconsistent with the decision reason's rule. Thus, the individual did not use the skewness-based decision reason.",
